1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,890
Mappa is a Linux-first workstation for offline maps.

2
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:09,135
It is built with Rust, Tauri and MapLibre, ships as a single binary,

3
00:00:09,255 --> 00:00:12,528
and keeps working when the network does not.

4
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:23,338
Pan and zoom a GPU-rendered map, switch between satellite, topographic and street basemaps,

5
00:00:23,458 --> 00:00:27,690
or connect your own XYZ, WMS and WMTS sources.

6
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:36,461
The layer stack works like a photo editor: basemaps at the bottom, your own sources,

7
00:00:36,581 --> 00:00:39,825
vector layers and offline packs above them.

8
00:00:39,945 --> 00:00:44,050
Drag to reorder, fade with opacity, hide with the eye.

9
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:52,242
For the field, download a region and pack it into one MBTiles or PMTiles file.

10
00:00:52,362 --> 00:00:57,236
The pack contains every tile, so the map opens without a network,

11
00:00:57,356 --> 00:01:00,770
and the same file can be shared with the team.

12
00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:07,401
Draw lines, polygons and circles, measure distance and area,

13
00:01:07,521 --> 00:01:13,530
and keep everything in the project as objects with names, folders and descriptions.

14
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:22,971
Load a DEM — SRTM, ASCII grid or a GeoTIFF — and get hillshade, contour lines,

15
00:01:23,091 --> 00:01:27,706
terrain profiles and minimum clearance for a route.

16
00:01:30,030 --> 00:01:35,233
For radio planning, pick two points, set the antenna heights and frequency,

17
00:01:35,353 --> 00:01:41,550
and Mappa computes line of sight, the first Fresnel zone and a viewshed over the terrain.

18
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:50,609
Scanned paper maps can be georeferenced with control points: affine, Helmert,

19
00:01:50,729 --> 00:01:58,270
polynomial or thin-plate spline, then exported as a GeoTIFF or COG that opens in QGIS.

20
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:08,852
Markers become a mission: takeoff, waypoints, return to launch, a geofence and a survey grid,

21
00:02:08,972 --> 00:02:12,998
exported as a QGroundControl plan, KML or KMZ.

22
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:23,149
Mappa receives MAVLink v1 and v2 telemetry over UDP, verifies the CRC, shows position,

23
00:02:23,269 --> 00:02:28,880
heading and altitude, records the track and exports it as GPX.

24
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,749
Field mode enlarges every control,

25
00:02:33,869 --> 00:02:39,480
raises contrast and keeps the screen awake on a tablet or a small laptop.

26
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,076
Mappa is open source under Apache 2.0.

27
00:02:45,196 --> 00:02:50,080
Build it, test it in the field, and tell us what breaks.
